      "summary": ": 31 Aug 2026 – Cardrona is closed for the day after winds increased and the forecast gave no indication of easing. The mountain is currently reporting -6°C, with winds of 58 km/h and gusts reaching 113 km/h. Light snow showers have accompanied the strong southwest flow, while the resort says conditions remain firm across the mountain and variable off-piste. All lifts and listed terrain are closed today, including Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express, Willow’s Quad and Wells Pipe Platter. The nine terrain-park areas are also closed. The access roads require chains on all vehicles from Valley View, with an active road hazard advisory in place. Snow cover is 100 cm at the 1800m weather station, and the resort has recorded 2 cm in the last 24 hours and 53 cm over seven days. The current closure follows increased winds and the resort will try again tomorrow.",
