      "summary": ": 31 Aug 2026 – Treble Cone is open in Home Basin, which is sheltered from the worst of the weather, while the Saddle remains closed in gale-force southwest winds. The light is fairly flat under high cloud, with scattered cloud between periods of blue sky and snow showers possible through the day. It is currently -4°C, with winds around 43 km/h and gusts to 82 km/h. The Home Basin Express and Beginner Platter are open. The Saddle Quad is closed because winds at the Saddle are gusting above 100 km/h. On-trail conditions are skiing well, with plenty of fresh cord and Lower Camel groomed from Main Street for the first time this season. Off-trail snow remains a mixed bag with considerable lumpy crust, so care is required away from groomed terrain. All three car parks are currently full, although the access road has reopened. Chains must be carried because snow is in the forecast and an active road hazard advisory remains in place. Backcountry Access is open, while Skinning Access is closed.",
